# Where the account's logins and keys are kept, relative to its home: one glob a line (* within a folder's name only,
# no braces). The security watcher watches each file that matches (CREDENTIALS, amethystora-audit-home-rules, with each
# agent profile's logins from /usr/share/amethystora/agent-paths added), and an agent's sandbox hides each one
# (amethystora-agent-tools, sandbox.rs). A login added here is in both the same day, and in the Vault's usual places
# (USUAL in apps/vault-service/src/protect.rs and apps/vault/src/page/protect.rs, which tests hold to this list), the
# browsers' aside. Files, never a folder: an audit rule watches files. A name with a space cannot be one, since no
# rule's path can hold it: such a secret is a hidden line of agent-paths alone (Bitwarden's "Bitwarden CLI").
